# Runebook

Local markdown notes at `projects/runebook.sh/`.

## Crates

- `crates/runebook` owns the vault, note ids, wiki links, and the in-memory index.
- `crates/runebook-app` owns the GPUI window. Do not put file rules in the app crate.

## Vault

- A vault root contains `runebook.toml` (`schema_version = 1`).
- A note is a `*.md` file. `NoteId` is the relative path without `.md`, with `/` separators.
- A media file beside a note uses a video, audio, or image extension: `mp4`, `webm`, `mkv`, `mov`, `mp3`, `wav`, `ogg`, `m4a`, `flac`, `png`, `jpg`, `jpeg`, `gif`, `webp`.
- Folder delete removes those files. Any other non-note file still blocks folder delete.
- A preview link to a media file opens that file. The path must stay inside the vault.
- Skip hidden paths and symlinks. Do not follow a symlink out of the vault.
- There is no sidecar database. The index is rebuilt from the files.
- User config is `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/runebook/config.toml`. It stores `last_vault`, `microphone`, `theme`, and `note_view`.

## Links

Resolve `[[target]]` in this order:

1. Exact `NoteId`
2. Unique file stem, only when `target` has no `/`

`[[target|alias]]` shows `alias` and still resolves `target`.

## App

- Call `gpui_kit::init` before any GPUI Kit control.
- The source pane is the Kit `Editor`. The preview pane is Kit markdown.
- The window shows the preview until the user flips to the source.
- Autosave is debounced. Also flush on note switch and window close.
